cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DT-GSK: Dimension-Tiered Gaining-Sharing Knowledge Optimization"
message: >-
  If you use this software or its benchmark evidence, please cite both the
  software (this file) and the accompanying manuscript listed under
  preferred-citation. If you use the GSK-family baselines re-implemented here,
  please also cite their original sources, listed under references.
type: software
version: "2.40"
date-released: 2026-09-02
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MostafaMassoud/DT-GSK"
# No DOI field. Author decision 2026-08-01 (D-0037): no Zenodo deposit and no
# repository DOI are created for this work. The article DOI is assigned by
# Algorithms (MDPI) after acceptance and belongs to the article, not to this
# software record. Keep the version field above equal to the tag this file
# ships inside (gated by papers/scripts/validate_citation_cff.py).
abstract: >-
  Reference Python implementation of DT-GSK (Dimension-Tiered Gaining-Sharing
  Knowledge Optimization) together with six re-implemented GSK-family
  baselines (GSK, AGSK, APGSK, FDB-AGSK, ATMALS-GSK, eGSK) and adapters for
  five CEC benchmark suites (CEC2011, CEC2013, CEC2013LSGO, CEC2017, CEC2020).
  DT-GSK resolves control by dimension rather than at a single operating
  point: an adaptive scaffold serves every tier, a deterministic budget-exact
  final refinement, searching the shipped eigenframe basis, runs from D = 50 upward, and the GSK vector-update
  equations are retained, with an exploratory interaction-structure memory
  learned from accepted moves at no extra evaluations supplying the refinement
  basis. The repository ships the full reproducibility chain used in the
  accompanying study: pinned seed schedules, a unified Threefry random-number
  stream, immutable evidence releases, a pre-registered statistical analysis
  plan, and the validation and freeze tooling that binds every reported number
  to a committed artifact. All reported standings are scoped to the
  seven-member GSK-family panel.
keywords:
  - metaheuristic optimization
  - gaining-sharing knowledge
  - dimension-tiered adaptive configuration selection
  - deterministic final refinement
  - adaptive operator selection
  - population-size reduction
  - CEC benchmark suites
  - nonparametric statistical comparison
  - reproducibility
